WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.002
-There's so much good stuff
happening this summer.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.303
I'm reading.
I'm getting into that.

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:08.274
There's good TV. I'm watching
my "Below Deck Med."

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.742
Is it Med? Yeah.

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:11.878
Captain Sandy is the greatest.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.847
I'm watching --
"Big Brother" is good.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.482
-Yeah!
-Right? It is good.

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:19.185
There's so many good
documentaries out there.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.853
Quest's "Summer of Soul"
is available.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:23.556
That's out right now on Hulu.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.659
It's unbelievable.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.328
But, you know, I'm a big fan of
reality shows.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:29.462
So, I just heard about this.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.731
There's a new show on Fox
they're developing

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.399
called "Mouse Trap,"

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:37.737
and it's based on
the Hasbro game Mouse Trap.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.339
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, I got to be --

00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:42.041
I'm having a hard time
imagining it because...

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.109
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.677
...a TV show based on
a board game.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.545
I mean, I'm serious.

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:48.881
I don't have a clue
what they would look like.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:51.651
[ Laughter ]
It seems like a huge risk.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:55.054
I mean, who's in charge of
this operation, you know?

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.289
Who's the mastermind?

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:00.193
You know, I can't even guess
who would do this.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.895
Some people think
it's a trivial pursuit.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:05.698
Like complete balderdash,
you know?

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:09.269
It really does boggle my mind
because I'm not convinced

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.304
it's up to par, cheesy
as that might sound.

00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:20.546
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:24.350
And this could get me in trouble
because it's taboo to say.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.020
But the premise just doesn't
connect for me.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.422
[ Laughter ]
And if someone asked me to be

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:33.026
on the show, I'd say "ew, no,"
because I don't know...

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.694
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.597
...anything about board games.
Sorry!

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.099
[ Cheers and applause ]

